# Sprint 10 – Windows Group Policy Hardening & Endpoint Security

## Completed
- Created a dedicated Group Policy Object (GPO) named **Workstation Hardening - Sprint 10**.
- Linked the GPO to the **Workstations** Organizational Unit (OU).
- Configured Microsoft Defender Antivirus security policies.
- Enabled Microsoft Defender Real-Time Protection.
- Enabled Defender Behavior Monitoring.
- Enabled scanning of downloaded files and attachments.
- Configured scheduled antivirus scanning.
- Configured Windows Defender Firewall for Domain, Private, and Public profiles.
- Enforced inbound firewall protection while preserving outbound communication.
- Verified continued Splunk Universal Forwarder communication after firewall policy changes.
- Configured automatic Windows Update installation policies.
- Prevented automatic reboot while users are logged in.
- Configured removable storage write restrictions through Group Policy.
- Managed local Administrator membership using Group Policy Preferences.
- Configured User Account Control (UAC) security settings.
- Applied the new Group Policy to WIN11-01.
- Validated Group Policy deployment using `gpresult`.
- Verified Microsoft Defender configuration through PowerShell.
- Verified Windows Firewall status through PowerShell.
- Verified local administrator membership.
- Confirmed Splunk Universal Forwarder and Sysmon remained operational after hardening.
- Generated post-hardening Windows and Sysmon telemetry.
- Verified security telemetry continued flowing into Splunk.
- Backed up the completed Group Policy Object.
- Created VMware snapshots documenting the hardened baseline.

